          "ResourceName": null,
          "Children": [
            {
              "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
              "Text": "GRDC funded CSP00187: Optimised Canola Profitability project investigated tactical agronomic decisions and the physiology of yield and oil formation in canola and how they are affected by variety,\n\nenviroment and management (G x E x M).\n\n \n\nThe project conducted > 50 experiments between 2014 and 2018 at 18 locations in south-eastern Australian canola growing regions (NSW, Vic, SA). Experiments investigated cultivar interactions with TOS_index, Plant density, water supply, N rate and timing of application.\n\n \n\n \n\nContact: Julianne Lilley, John Kirkegaard (CSIRO)",
              "Name": "Memo",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [],
              "Enabled": false,
              "ReadOnly": false
            },
